Well,  as long as I'm going to bother running a poll,  I might as well
post the results when it's done...

The questions were:

1)  Regarding movement onto water,  would you like:

A - No confirmation (current implementation)
B - confirmation (as in for peaceful monsters,  default ON)
C - confirmation (ditto,  except default OFF)
D - confirmation as a compile option -- not part of the original question
    set,  but specified by several voters

Votes for:
  A	17	 (26.6%)
  B	31.5	 (49.2%)
  C	12.5	 (19.5%)
  D	3         (4.7%)
  Total 64	(100.0%)

Clearly,  there is popular sentiment for confirmation.


2) Regarding attacking particular monsters (like floating eyes),
   would you like:

E - No confirmation (current implementation)
F - optional confirmations for each monster name (default off,  of course)
G - optional confirmation IF compile-time option  -- not asked originally,
    but specified by one voter

Votes for:
  E	25	 (39.7%)
  F     37	 (58.7%)
  G     1	  (1.6%)
  Total 63	(100.0%)

Again, we have support for the confirmation,  although it is not as
strong as we had for water confirmation.

---

My own votes were for C & F.  I play nethack for fun,  and drowning or
running into a floating eye just because I have to play on a remote system
is extremely annoying.  If I have to die,  I would rather go out fighting...

The only criticism I got for running the poll was the message that was
posted;  I got no negative e-mail (and obviously 63 people who had some
support for the idea) about it.  I also got my first email ever from
Denmark and West Germany,  so email-wise it broadened me...

